    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line on successful owner creation, via a logger named `AUDIT`, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nI implemented this in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`), placing the log call right after `clinicService.createOwner(...)` succeeds \u2014 at that point the owner has been persisted (so `id` is populated) and the service has assigned `customerCode`, while `registrationDate` was already normalized earlier in the method.\n\nChanges in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added SLF4J imports and a `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n- Emitted `AUDIT.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate())` after a successful create.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes, and the build is green.",
